session:pr689Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #625 asked for SWRL DLSafeRule(...) parsing in owl_functional_parser, filed on the premise that owl_ontology had no representation for SWRL rules at all. Checked provenance for crate:owl_functional_parser (no results) and crate:manchester_parser (PR #158, #288) first, then read provenance/summaries/pr-636.ttl directly (issue #498, PR #636), which showed that premise had gone stale: #636 already added owl_ontology::SwrlRule/Atom/AtomArg plus Ontology.rules for manchester_parser's own Rule: frames, landing after #625 was filed but before this PR started. Reused those types directly rather than inventing new ones, as the issue itself anticipated as a possibility. Also verified via WebFetch/WebSearch that DLSafeRule(...) is not actually part of the W3C OWL 2 Functional-Style Syntax spec (the issue's own '#11 of the spec' framing was wrong) -- it's an OWL API/Protege convention layered on the SWRL submission's abstract syntax; confirmed the concrete grammar (Body/Head/ClassAtom/DataRangeAtom/ObjectPropertyAtom/DataPropertyAtom/BuiltInAtom/SameIndividualAtom/DifferentIndividualsAtom, IArg/DArg) against that source before writing any parser code, and corrected the plan doc and CLAUDE.md's stale framing. Mapped the seven functional-syntax atom kinds onto the existing three-variant Atom enum: ClassAtom and the property atoms map directly; ObjectPropertyAtom(ObjectInverseOf(P), x, y) is represented by swapping the two arguments onto P rather than needing a new type; BuiltInAtom is reachable at any arity (including 2) here, unlike Manchester's arity-based guess, since functional syntax's keyword is never ambiguous; DataRangeAtom/SameIndividualAtom/DifferentIndividualsAtom have no faithful existing encoding and were added as three new Atom variants, with a skip-and-log::warn! arm added to manchester_parser's serializer for the two atom kinds its own Rule: grammar can't produce. TDD: wrote the plan doc addendum first (mapping table + grammar), then ignored tests in a new swrl_rule.rs and additions to serialize_roundtrip.rs, then implemented rule.rs, lib.rs's axiom/rule interleaving via a new Item enum, and serialize.rs's DLSafeRule(...) emission, unignoring tests as they went green. All tests passed on first full run after implementation; only cargo fmt needed a follow-up commit." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:689 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr689 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr689Decision .

session:pr689Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Reused owl_ontology::Atom (from #498/PR #636) by extending it with three new variants (DataRangeAtom, SameIndividualAtom, DifferentIndividualsAtom) rather than defining a separate, functional-syntax-specific atom type." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered giving owl_functional_parser its own parallel Atom/AtomArg types matching the functional-syntax grammar one-to-one (all seven keywords as distinct variants, since unlike Manchester's ambiguous concrete syntax, functional syntax never needs to guess an atom's kind). Rejected: it would fragment SwrlRule.body/head's element type between the two parsers, defeating the whole point of #498 landing shared types 'the same target type manchester_parser produces' pattern this crate already follows for Ontology itself; downstream consumers (a future reasoner over SWRL rules) would need to handle two incompatible atom representations. The three-variant gap is small enough (DataRangeAtom/Same/DifferentIndividualsAtom) that extending the existing enum, with Manchester's serializer skip-and-warn for the unreachable cases, was cheaper than a parallel type hierarchy." .
